NOT ACCEPTED

  Nothing else in this directory is an accepted theorem. formal/spec holds
  skeletons that no checker has read.

  No checker has accepted the hardware bridge. SpecSafety is conditional on
  two premises, and no formal tool discharges either:

    - HashInjective is an ASSUME. Real soundness is SHA-256 collision
      resistance, which is a cryptographic assumption, not a theorem. The
      finite instance verifies the premise mechanically for its own toy Hash,
      which shows the premise is satisfiable -- not that SHA-256 satisfies it.

    - Infer purity on real hardware is a CONJECTURE. The spec treats Infer as
      a function. A GPU with non-deterministic reduction order is not one.

  An attacker attacks the bridge, not the model. Proving SpecSafety moved the
  remaining risk entirely into these two premises; it did not reduce it.

This file is pinned by config/architecture.json (formal_proof.must_contain) and
checked by scripts/check_architecture.py. The pinned string is the hardware
bridge disclaimer, so the disclaimer cannot be dropped to make the repository
look stronger than it is.
